The 3- and 10-page editions are built, from the storyteller's scripts as they stood at 04:42 today, in the lab's look (type A, Crown Quarto, standard colour), the signed title on the title page:
- manuscript/editions/03/: three pages and the series page at the back (SP1); 6 PDF pages with the title page and contents.
- manuscript/editions/10/: ten pages, the series page moved to the back; 12 PDF pages.
publishing/edition.py makes them from a script: each page its own page, the cast bar, the words box and the band as styled blocks, the developer's %%%% markers and the script's header and notes for the writers left out, the script's own sources at the end. No words changed. To rebuild: python3 publishing/edition.py 03 && python3 publishing/build_book.py --book manuscript/editions/03/Book.txt --name one-human-nine-agents-edition-03 --stamp "One Human, Nine Agents, Nineteen Hours: the 3-page edition, 2 November 2026" (and the same with 10).
The PDFs land in _site/manuscript/one-human-nine-agents-edition-03.pdf and -10.pdf (not tracked; CI or the command above makes them). The title and subtitle are in publishing/metadata.yaml, so the book, the sample and the editions all carry it; LEANPUB.md names it, and the slug one-human-nine-agents was free on Leanpub at 05:15 (a check, not a reservation). The listing's draft (publishing/listing.md) is next. Security and the researcher have the editions to read.

